title: 'cumulus: add support for signed scheduling info'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |
    V3 candidates built by the slot-based collator now carry a signed scheduling info in
    their scheduling proof, which previously went out without one. The collator signs the
    core selector, the claim queue offset, its approved peer id and the internal scheduling
    parent with the Aura key that won the slot.

    An initial submission stays valid without the signature, since core selection is taken
    from the block's UMP signals, while a resubmission will not be. Signing happens here
    for every V3 candidate because that is what resubmissions will do by default once they
    land, for any core whose resubmittable segment is not empty. A collator that cannot
    sign skips the slot.
crates:
- name: cumulus-client-consensus-aura
  bump: patch
- name: cumulus-primitives-core
  bump: minor
- name: cumulus-pallet-parachain-system
  bump: none
